{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482424-ssl-down-for-anyone-else-on-the-site","id":1482424,"title":"SSL down for anyone else on the site ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-30T17:22:54-07:00","id":1482424,"title":"SSL down for anyone else on the site ?","content":"I went to log into the site and chrome is telling me SSL is not secure for this site. Is anyone else getting that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T17:32:28-07:00","id":1482426,"title":"","content":"I'm totally not a techy, but I think the Not Secure exclamation-triangle I always see at the left of the address just means &quot;information you share with this website may be shared&quot;, as in, it's a forum where members (identified by username) can read each others posts. I don't know who you are and you can read this reply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T20:20:05-07:00","id":1482447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482424-ssl-down-for-anyone-else-on-the-site?p=1482426#post1482426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm totally not a techy, but I think the Not Secure exclamation-triangle I always see at the left of the address just means &quot;information you share with this website may be shared&quot;, as in, it's a forum where members (identified by username) can read each others posts. I don't know who you are and you can read this reply.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not what it means.<br /> <br /> To receive this message it usually means you're trying to access through the HTTP<u><b>S</b></u> protocol or in some other way trying to access as if this was a Secure site, but it isn't. It may be that Chrome is starting to assume all site should be Secure and giving this warning at any non-Secure site, IDK since I don't use Chrome anymore, mostly I use Vivaldi nowadays.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a> those warnings on Not Secure sites have nothing to do with the site being a forum. Actually, by all accounts, this forum <b>should</b> be Secure, it isn't because it is old and full of bugs that no one addresses.<br /> <br /> A Secure Site encrypts data in a certain way during transmission, both from and into your computer. That way a third party intercepting the data can't make heads or tails of it before it reaches its destination.<br /> <br /> Why it matters here? First, to protect your account so no one can steal your password through data probing. Also to keep your PMs, Flags and other non-public tasks non-public. Also to avoid that this third party intercept your posting and edits it before it goes into the site. And finally that because some of the data packages may contain other information like timestamps and IP addresses that give the hacker more info about you.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't really care a lot about it here, I am here after all. But this information may be relevant for your internet usage elsewhere. Do not take lightly this aspect, this is about securing the data transfer and most sites should be Secure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T20:38:45-07:00","id":1482451,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, a bit disconcerting. Good to know. Thank you. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:10:41-07:00","id":1482522,"title":"","content":"I am a web developer and regularly involved in setting up websites to run on HTTPS (which is dependent on the site having an SSL certificate). Based on that experience I can confirm that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> is correct.<br /> <br /> The folks running the forum tried switching it to https a few years back and ran into a lot of problems which effectively broke the site and they didn't have access to the resources that would have been needed to pursue a solution so they switched it back to non-https. That is how it has been ever since. <br /> <br /> Mainstream, modern browsers will generally throw an error and default to blocking access if a site doesn't have an SSL certificate because the current industry stance is that all websites should have SSL for security and user confidence purposes. You can generally tell the browser to ignore it on any given site, but it can take some wandering through the browser's settings to do that since it is 'discouraged' for safety reasons.<br /> <br /> The Onyx Path site not using HTTPS/SSL is one of the reasons I make certain I don't reuse this password anywhere else (which you should do anyways) and I assume that anything I view here is 'public' which generally is no big deal for me on this site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T17:15:56-07:00","id":1482555,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting that a &quot;no SSL&quot; error is different from a &quot;expired Certificate&quot; error. Those certificates must be updated regularly, about 1 or 2 years last time I saw, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1039\" data-vbnamecard=\"1039\">Brennanhawkwood</a> can correct me there, and sometimes the owner of a site simply doesn't update them properly. It is still safer to deal with an expired Certificate than with no certificate, <b><u>IF</u></b> you really trust the site in question, but it is still sub-optimal.<br /> <br /> Most browsers will block a site with an expired certificate on spot, but let you chose to ignore the issue at the same page if you want. Don't do that if you don't really, really trust and need that site.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T12:13:17-07:00","id":1482810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482424-ssl-down-for-anyone-else-on-the-site?p=1482555#post1482555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting that a &quot;no SSL&quot; error is different from a &quot;expired Certificate&quot; error. Those certificates must be updated regularly, about 1 or 2 years last time I saw, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1039\" data-vbnamecard=\"1039\">Brennanhawkwood</a> can correct me there, and sometimes the owner of a site simply doesn't update them properly. It is still safer to deal with an expired Certificate than with no certificate, <b><u>IF</u></b> you really trust the site in question, but it is still sub-optimal.<br /> <br /> Most browsers will block a site with an expired certificate on spot, but let you chose to ignore the issue at the same page if you want. Don't do that if you don't really, really trust and need that site.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correct. In my experience multi-year SSL certificates are becoming less and less common as there are security issues associated with not resetting the certificates often enough. Single year certs are better for security... but likely to result in more oops moments with missed renewals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T07:14:47-07:00","id":1483585,"title":"","content":"About one third of the time, when I go to Like a reply, it says, &quot;people who liked this post: no permission&quot;, as if I were trying to find out this information by clicking the outer edge of the Like button. I have to center my mouse and click again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T19:03:49-07:00","id":1483673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482424-ssl-down-for-anyone-else-on-the-site?p=1483585#post1483585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About one third of the time, when I go to Like a reply, it says, &quot;people who liked this post: no permission&quot;, as if I were trying to find out this information by clicking the outer edge of the Like button. I have to center my mouse and click again.</div> </div> </div> </div>The forum's engine has an optional feature where by clicking in the dialog box with the number of likes you see the list of users that liked the post, but here this option is disabled for the general users (it may be available for mods and/or admins, idk).<br /> <br /> Since the option exists, whenever you click in the dialog instead of the actual Like hitbox, the system will recognize that as a try to access this information and process it as normal, since it is a valid request despite being denied in the next processing step.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it is possible to disable the option and extend the Like hitbox, and I currently doubt it can be implemented here in particular, given the current state of the forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":", because it was a weird wording. 06-11-2022, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T19:55:27-07:00","id":1483681,"title":"","content":"There are definitely things I like about the layout of the forum that are superior to some others which I cannot stand. The grey bar around the user profile takes the full width of the screen, according some importance to the person posting. You see their join date and number of posts, which can be an indicator of how important the subject is to the member replying. If they have been around for a long time, but have made very few posts, it gives the impression that they mostly read and only participate when the subject is near and dear to them. A very high number of posts indicates a genuine interest in the games lines, generally.<br /> <br /> The grey bar also relieves my eyes of over-whiteness that I see on other forums. I can't remember which one I was reading recently, but it was just a white space with indented comments. Despite being curious enough about the subject to log in, I couldn't stay, because of the eye-burn and lack of design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}